              <span class="text-cyan-400">🇦🇷</span> Argentina: MEP & Blue Dollar Dynamics
            </h3>
            <p class="text-xs text-slate-300">
              Argentina has historically maintained multiple exchange rates due to strict capital controls (cepo cambiario):
            </p>
            <ul class="text-xs space-y-2 list-disc list-inside text-slate-400">
              <li><strong class="text-slate-200">Dólar MEP (Electronic Market Rate):</strong> Applied automatically to foreign Visa/Mastercard payments. When you swipe a foreign credit card at a café in Palermo, the transaction clears at near the parallel market rate, eliminating the historic need to carry suitcases of cash.</li>
              <li><strong class="text-slate-200">Dólar Blue (Informal Cash Rate):</strong> Physical exchange rate negotiated in cash exchange houses (cuevas) or via Western Union pickups. Blue cash often yields a small premium (2–6%) over MEP.</li>
              <li><strong class="text-slate-200">Crypto Rails (USDT):</strong> Most digital nomads in Buenos Aires convert USDT/USDC directly into physical Argentine Pesos (ARS) or crisp $100 USD bills through OTC crypto brokers at 1% fees.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>

          <!-- Colombia Currency Deep Dive -->
