            </p>
            <ul class="text-xs space-y-2 list-disc list-inside text-slate-400">
              <li><strong class="text-slate-200">TRM (Tasa Representativa del Mercado):</strong> The daily official exchange rate determined by the Central Bank (Banco de la República). Credit cards, wire transfers, and ATMs convert at the TRM.</li>
              <li><strong class="text-slate-200">ATM Optimization:</strong> BBVA and Davivienda ATMs in Colombia generally do not charge local ATM operator fees for foreign debit cards (Wise, Schwab). Avoid Servibanca ATMs which charge hefty per-transaction surcharges.</li>
              <li><strong class="text-slate-200">Decline DCC (Dynamic Currency Conversion):</strong> Always elect to be billed in Colombian Pesos (COP) at point-of-sale terminals to let your home bank perform the interbank conversion rather than accepting the merchant terminal's inflated USD rate.</li>
            </ul>
